false},"body":"## IMGPROC-GNATDOC-009R1 — CORE_POLICY_REVIEW_REQUIRED\n\n**Incomplete production migration. Not production-ready. Production remains unchanged.** Existing PR updated in place; no new PR, force-push, merge, upstream modification or feature-branch publication.\n\n### Complete Core reconciliation\n- **586 occurrences / 14 distinct Core types**, reconstructed with the unchanged legacy resolver. Every occurrence retains source declaration identity, native page/anchor/snippet/hash, exact type mark and offsets, Core owner, old package URL, proposed direct-fragment URL and source/native/hosted proof.\n- Exact indexed Core **0.5.0** (`f8aef00c5366b4275ccd3d934f9c73ea5b83cd4f`) freshly acquired/built. All src bytes equal the actual Alire-resolved dependency. Fresh genuine GNATdoc 26.0.0 native output has empty diagnostics.\n- All 14 referenced declarations match pinned and hosted Git sources, genuine native profiles/anchors and hosted snippets. Actual HTTPS matches **all 209 files** of immutable Core review artifact **12238050173**, ZIP SHA-256 `fd328d27efc3196b5861d11c73561c2d22451e2a0fcf2b6477d7c6e0f853cc37`, source `aa8a378ab614e9a5fc4f43765cd3ff1bbcf6a44d`, successful Pages deployment **7190346920**. Unversioned Pages is mutable; only referenced-type compatibility is claimed.\n- The official unmodified enhancer passes inventory/enhance/verify using explicit HTTPS page-plus-fragment URLs. All **586** output occurrences match exact identity/offset/label/URL. Two fresh enhancements match; repeat enhancement is byte-idempotent.\n- **350 local links** preserve the original 348. The two additions are independently source-proven constant type marks: Background_Label to Component_Label, and Default_Morphology_Border to the public partial view of Morphology_Border_Value. Filename-plus-fragment destinations resolve to the original genuine anchors.\n- **329** exact source-ordered operation entries; **1596/1596** documented elements; zero documentation warnings; empty baselines; six examples compile and execute unchanged.\n- Unintercepted Chromium covers all 14 live destinations and generated keyboard links in eight desktop/mobile, light/dark, JS-on/off combinations, with visible declaration and iframe Back/Forward checks. Failed probe attempts remain alongside the completed report; optional authentic Core favicon 404 is explicitly classified, not intercepted.\n- Seven R1 tests pass with full-candidate controls, including wrong URL/owner/offset/label, duplicate occurrence, altered anchor/profile and generated identity rejection. Existing 13 release controls pass with installed tamper checks enabled. Installer implementation unchanged.\n\n### Independent policy decision required before promotion\nAll 586 proposed links change:\n1. Package-overview query navigation to a specific native declaration fragment.\n2. Legacy target=_top to no target attribute: Core loads inside the Imgproc iframe; the outer bookmark continues naming Imgproc.\n\nThe second change is demonstrated in a real browser. It is not an upstream defect claim. Task section 5 requires stopping when material navigation changes lack independent approval. The proposal and policy-review record explicitly have approval=false. Review must accept this behavior or request separately reviewed upstream support preserving top-level navigation. No HTML rewrite, injected script, local fork or monkey-patch is used.\n\n### Preservation and remaining gates\nMerged PR #80 is reconciled at main `3b44846687354f344d078104fe6101bfb7997534`. Its renderer/tests, all earlier 009 evidence, historical 008/008C authority/workflow, library sources, Alire manifest, production generator and main-only Pages deployment safeguards remain unchanged. The PR-only acquisition workflow adds R1 negative controls and non-deployable evidence upload, not production promotion.\n\nFull authored/shared site qualification, complete production browser/security matrix, workflow promotion, Pages candidate inventory and actual final candidate artifact equality remain unperformed past the policy gate. Deployment/live acceptance remain post-merge. No READY_FOR_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW claim.\n\nEvidence: docs/evidence/gnatdoc009/r1/README.md, core-destination-proposal.json, candidate-reconciliation.json, core-candidate-browser-final.json, policy-review.json and additive sha256.json. Final immutable feature head/tree and exact-head hosted outcomes are recorded in the checkpoint comment.\n\nLeave PR #81 open, non-draft, unmerged, auto-merge disabled.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-21T04:35:47Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T05:03:20Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"9bc550fb5235fa7cc829e15dd4d902a87f15a8d3","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"zackboll:docs/009-production-shared-enhancer-v0.1.0","ref":"docs/009-production-shared-enhancer-v0.1.0","repo":{"id":1356565149,"node_id":"R_kgDOUNuKnQ","name":"opencv_imgproc_ada","full_name":"zackboll/opencv_imgproc_ada","owner":{"login":"zackboll","id":4860920,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NjA5MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4860920?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zackboll","html_url":"https://github.com/zackboll","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zackboll/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zackboll/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zackboll/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zackboll/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zackboll/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zackboll/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zackboll/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zackboll/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zackboll/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","si